---
source: crates/pogo-cli/tests/cli.rs
expression: help
---
Capture serial output until a pattern, fault, or deadline

Usage: pogo serial capture [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --reset
          Reset into run mode first and capture from the first boot byte

      --baud <N>
          Baud rate

      --until <REGEX>
          Stop with success when a line matches (repeatable)

      --fail-on <REGEX>
          Stop with TARGET_FAULT when a line matches (repeatable)

      --no-default-fail-patterns
          Don't use the built-in panic/abort/brownout patterns

      --settle <DURATION>
          Keep reading this long after an --until match to catch late crashes

      --max-lines <N>
          Maximum lines returned; extra lines are omitted from the middle
          
          [default: 500]

      --max-line-len <N>
          Maximum characters per line; longer lines are truncated
          
          [default: 1000]

      --parser <PARSER>
          Log line parser
          
          [default: auto]
          [possible values: auto, esp-idf, rust-log, raw]

      --elf <PATH>
          ELF used to symbolize backtraces

      --raw
          Keep ANSI escape codes

      --record <FILE>
          Save the raw byte stream with timestamps as JSONL

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

  -V, --version
          Print version

Global options:
  -d, --device <SELECTOR>
          Target device: alias, USB serial, port, or "auto"

      --probe <SELECTOR>
          Probe device [default: "probe" alias, else auto]

  -f, --format <FORMAT>
          Output format [default: human]
          
          [env: POGO_FORMAT=]
          [possible values: human, json, jsonl]

      --config <PATH>
          Config file
          
          [env: POGO_CONFIG=]

      --timeout <DURATION>
          Overall deadline for this command, e.g. 500ms, 10s, 2m

      --wait-lock <DURATION>
          Wait for a busy device instead of failing

      --dry-run
          Describe what a mutating command would do; change nothing

  -v, --verbose...
          More logs on stderr (repeatable)

  -q, --quiet
          Errors only on stderr

      --no-color
          Disable colors

Reads lines until an --until pattern matches, a fault is detected, or the deadline
(default 10s). Built-in fail patterns catch panics, aborts, brownouts, and watchdogs.

Examples:
  pogo serial capture --reset --until READY --timeout 15s -f json
  pogo serial capture --fail-on 'E \(\d+\) app' --elf app.elf
  pogo serial capture --timeout 3s --record session.jsonl

Exit codes: 0 matched (or completed with no --until), 4 timeout, 6 device vanished (eof),
7 target fault, 9 device busy

JSON data: { device, outcome: matched|completed|fault|timeout|eof, matched, line_count,
omitted_lines, boot_count, resets, panic, lines: [ { t_ms, level, tag, device_ts_ms, text } ] }
